WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.400
- [Narrator] Between the
snow-covered mountains

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.970
deep in Gangwon Province in South Korea

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.840
sits one of the country's
hottest spa crazes,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.800
and we mean literally hot.

00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:25.624
(bouncy electronic music)

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:35.340
(bouncy piano music)

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.100
- [Narrator] Charcoal
played an important role

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.190
in Korean culture.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.850
Its use dates back over 2,600 years

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.690
to heat homes, cook food,
and ward off bad energy.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.100
Seo Jong-won and his father make charcoal

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.870
from oak wood that is
unique to this region.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.270
It's an arduous process
that starts and ends

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.420
with kilns or giant ovens.

00:01:24.499 --> 00:01:26.450
- [Narrator] The kilns
function as a traditional

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.880
Korean sauna, a treatment
that has been happening

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.710
for hundreds of years.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.873
Customers pay a small fee to spend time

00:01:32.873 --> 00:01:35.710
sweating out their
toxins in the hot rooms.

00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:14.110
- [Narrator] And a national
attraction it will stay.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.620
Seo Jong-won has no plans of slowing down

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.900
the family business.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.872
(lively, bouncy music)

00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:45.605
(bell ringing)

